    "description": "Salt-marsh traders who run Dhunmouth's quays and work the salt flats south of the city. Organised into salt-houses; loud, warm, theatrical hagglers for whom a bargain is a song sung by two people. Superstitious about the sea, which they love and curse in the same breath.",
