      "writable": true,
      "sound": "A sing-song, lilting speech that rises and falls like a tide-call: soft hissing sh, zh and z over long open vowels, almost no hard stops. Words end on a vowel or a breathy -sh. Haggling is half-sung; curses are hissed through the teeth; greetings are drawn out on the last vowel.",
