    "customs": [
      "Accepting a first price is an insult: a bargain must be sung back and forth at least three times.",
      "Deals are sealed by touching salted thumbs.",
      "Never whistle on a quay; it calls the sea's attention.",
      "A sea curse is always followed by spitting into the water, so the curse goes to the sea and not the boat."
    ],
    "food": "Brined mullet, samphire, flatbread baked on hot salt-stones, sour plum wine. Undyed linen, wide straw hats, salt-white headscarves; quay-masters wear brass weighing-chains as belts.",
    "holidays": [
      {
        "name": "Zhoa-Ani (First Salt)",
        "when": "first dry week of high summer, when the pans first crust",
        "description": "The first salt crust is raked at dawn; a handful goes back to the sea, the rest is tasted by every household. The quays close for the day and small debts are sung forgiven."
      }
